import theorem.PowerSystem.Synchronous.OscillationPhasor
import theorem.ParametricResonance.Wirtinger
import theorem.ParametricResonance.BlockAveragingDetuned

/-! # Parametric oscillations of TR-110's swing model: energy, phase angle and boundary

TR-110's linearized swing equation (§3.3) with a periodically varying synchronizing coefficient
`K_s(t)`. A sustained oscillation needs an energy source; the period energy balance of
`theorem/ParametricResonance/EnergyBalance.lean`, written in the report's variables, separates
the three mechanisms: no source (natural, `ξ = 0`), the mechanical power `ΔP_m` (forced), the pump
work of `K_s(t)` (parametric). For every free oscillation with `K_D = 0` the period average of
`ΔP_e Δω` vanishes, natural or parametric, so the phase-angle method of §3.3 — which reads the
damping from the part of `ΔP_e` in phase with `Δω` — sees `φ = π/2`, i.e. `ξ = 0`, on a sustained
parametric oscillation up to the harmonic content, even though `K_d > 0`. The boundary of the
half-frequency parametric oscillation is bounded rigorously from below for every modulation depth
(`ε ≥ ξ Ω / ω_n`, the Wirtinger–energy bound) and located to first order by the merged 2:1
averaging theorems (`ε > 4 √(ξ² + d²)`).

Model boundary.
* One generator, TR-110's linearized swing equation (3-8) with the electrical power deviation
  (3-9) at an operating point, continuous time, state `(Δδ, Δδ̇)`:
  `(2H/ω₀) Δδ̈ + (K_D/ω₀) Δδ̇ = ΔP_m − ΔP_e`, `ΔP_e(t) = K_s(t) Δδ + K_d Δω`, `Δω = Δδ̇/ω₀`,
  with the parameters `Params` (`H, ω₀, K_D, K_s, K_d`) of
  `theorem/PowerSystem/Synchronous/OscillationPhasor.lean` and the synchronizing coefficient
  replaced by a prescribed function of time `K_s(t)` (`frozen`: the report's parameters at the
  instant `t`). `K_d`, `K_D`, `H`, `ω₀` are constant; `ΔP_m(t)` is an arbitrary continuous
  input.
* The modulation `K_s(t)` is an external, prescribed periodic variation of the operating point,
  not generated by the oscillation itself: e.g. a periodic variation of the terminal or bus voltage
  magnitude or of the line reactance (`K_s ≈ E V cos δ₀ / X`), a periodically switched series
  compensation, or the double-frequency (`2ω`) torque and power ripple of an unbalanced network
  acting on the synchronizing torque. Its relative form is `K_s(t) = K_s (1 + ε p(t))`.
* Excluded, as in TR-110 §3.3: the nonlinear power-angle curve, AVR/PSS and network dynamics
  beyond the constants `K_s(t)`, `K_d`, multi-machine coupling, and the measurement (Prony)
  extraction of phasors; signals are exact functions of time.
* First-order boundary: the family `famParams`, `famKs` with damping, detuning and modulation all
  of order `ε` (stated with its scalings below); the Floquet statements are for its state matrix
  `(frozen …).stateMatrix` of (3-10) in the state `(Δδ, Δδ̇)`.

Source: IEEE PES TR-110 "Forced Oscillations in Power Systems" (2023) §3.3, eqs. (3-6)–(3-13)
(swing model, damping ratio (3-11), phase-angle method (3-12)–(3-13)) and §3.1 (intrinsic
damping of natural and forced oscillations); the parametric mechanism and its first instability tongue
(Landau–Lifshitz, Mechanics §27: `ẍ + 2λẋ + ω₀²(1 + h cos(2ω₀ + ε')t) x = 0` is unstable for
`(hω₀/4)² > (ε'/2)² + λ²`).

Corrections and sharpenings.
* TR-110 reads the damping of an oscillation from the phase angle between the `ΔP_e` and `Δω`
  phasors and separates natural from forced oscillations only. On a sustained parametric
  oscillation the in-phase part of the fundamental is not `K_d |Δω|` but is bounded by the
  harmonic tail (`parametric_inPhase_le`), so the method reports `φ ≈ π/2`, `ξ ≈ 0`, although
  `K_d > 0` (the pump work balances the damping power, `parametric_power_balance`).
* The first-order boundary `ε > 4√(ξ² + d²)` (`Ω = 2ω_n(1 + d)`) is not an exact threshold: it is
  what the averaging theorems give for the family with `ξ = εξ̂`, `d = εd̂`, depth `εη̂` as `ε → 0`
  (`firstOrder_stable`, `firstOrder_unstable`: `η̂² ≶ 16(ξ̂² + d̂²)`). For every depth the exact
  energy bound `ε ≥ ξΩ/ω_n` (`2ξ` at `Ω = 2ω_n`) holds (`halfFrequency_depth_ge`); it is half of
  the first-order value `4ξ` at zero detuning.

Results.
* `frozen`, `modulated_iff` — the modulated (3-8)–(3-9) is
  `M Δδ̈ + D Δδ̇ + K_s(t) Δδ = ΔP_m` with `M = 2H/ω₀`, `D = (K_d + K_D)/ω₀`.
* `elecPower`, `speedDev`, `electrical_energy` — over a common period `L` of the solution and of
  `K_s`: `∫₀ᴸ ΔP_e Δω = ∫₀ᴸ ΔP_m Δω − K_D ∫₀ᴸ Δω²` (from
  `ParametricResonance.EnergyBalance.energy_balance`);
  `free_electrical_energy` — for a free oscillation with `K_D = 0` it is zero, natural or
  parametric.
* `natural_dampingRatio_eq_zero` — constant `K_s`, `ΔP_m = 0`: every nonconstant periodic solution
  has `ξ = 0` (not only sinusoids).
* `parametric_power_balance` — `ΔP_m = 0`: `(K_d + K_D) ∫₀ᴸ Δω² = (1/(2ω₀)) ∫₀ᴸ K̇_s Δδ²`.
* `forced_power_phasor`, `forced_amplitude` — forced sinusoidal steady state, constant `K_s`
  (wave-1 phasors): `Re(F W̄) = (K_d + K_D) |W|²` (energy enters through `ΔP_m`) and
  `|D| = |F| / |K_s − MΩ² + jΩD|` (amplitude linear in `ΔP_m`); the angle method reads `ξ`
  correctly there (`OscillationPhasor.Params.dampingRatio_eq_angleDamping`).
* `inPhase_hasSum_zero`, `parametric_inPhase_le` — with `P_k`, `W_k` the Fourier coefficients of
  `ΔP_e`, `Δω` over the period: `Σ_k Re(P_k W̄_k) = 0`, hence
  `|P₁||W₁| |cos φ₁| ≤ |P₀||W₀|/2 + Σ_{k≥2} |P_k||W_k|` with `φ₁` the lag angle of the
  fundamental phasors; `halfFrequency_inPhase_le` — for a half-frequency oscillation the mean
  term vanishes.
* `natFreq`, `dampingRatio_div_natFreq`, `halfFrequency_depth_ge`, `halfFrequency_depth_ge_two` —
  a sustained half-frequency oscillation under `K_s(1 + ε cos Ωt)` needs `|ε| ≥ ξ Ω / ω_n`,
  `ω_n = √(ω₀K_s/(2H))`; at `Ω = 2ω_n`, `|ε| ≥ 2ξ`.
* `famParams`, `famKs`, `famParams_dampingRatio`, `famParams_natFreq`, `famKs_eq`,
  `fam_firstOrder` — the first-order family (pump `2ν₀`, `K_d = 4εHν₀ξ̂`, `K_D = 0`,
  `K_s(t) = (2H/ω₀) ν₀² (1 − 2εd̂ + εη̂ cos 2ν₀t)`) and its exact TR-110 quantities:
  `ξ = εξ̂/√(1 − 2εd̂)`, `ω_n = ν₀ √(1 − 2εd̂)`, relative depth `η = εη̂/(1 − 2εd̂)`, pump
  detuning `d = 1/√(1 − 2εd̂) − 1` (`2ν₀ = 2ω_n(1 + d)`); `ξ/ε → ξ̂`, `η/ε → η̂`, `d/ε → d̂`.
* `fam_stateMatrix`, `shift_fam`, `pump_fam` — the family's state matrix is
  `A₀c + ε(A₀' + Re{A₁ e^{j2ν₀t}})` with first-order eigenvalue shift `λ₁ = −ν₀ξ̂ − jν₀d̂` and pump
  `g = jν₀η̂/2` in the real modal coordinates of `A₀c`.
* `firstOrder_stable`, `firstOrder_unstable` — `BlockAveraging.physical_stable`/`_unstable`:
  `ξ̂ > 0`, `η̂² < 16(ξ̂² + d̂²)` gives Floquet stability, `16(ξ̂² + d̂²) < η̂²` Floquet
  instability of the swing model for all small `ε > 0`.
-/

noncomputable section
namespace powerlib.Synchronous.ParametricSwing

open Complex Set Function Filter Topology Matrix ComplexConjugate
open powerlib.Synchronous.OscillationPhasor
open powerlib.SpecialFunctions.PeriodicWaves

/-! ## The model with a time-varying synchronizing coefficient -/

/-- The report's parameters frozen at the instant `t`: the synchronizing coefficient replaced by
its value `K_s(t)`. -/
def frozen (p : Params) (Ks : ℝ → ℝ) (t : ℝ) : Params := { p with Ks := Ks t }

/-- The electrical power deviation signal `ΔP_e(t) = K_s(t) Δδ(t) + K_d Δω(t)`. -/
def elecPower (p : Params) (Ks δ δ' : ℝ → ℝ) (t : ℝ) : ℝ := (frozen p Ks t).Pe (δ t) (δ' t / p.ω₀)

/-- The per-unit speed deviation signal `Δω(t) = Δδ̇(t)/ω₀`. -/
def speedDev (p : Params) (δ' : ℝ → ℝ) (t : ℝ) : ℝ := δ' t / p.ω₀

variable {p : Params}

/-- The modulated swing equation (3-8)–(3-9) is `M Δδ̈ + D Δδ̇ + K_s(t) Δδ = ΔP_m`, `M = 2H/ω₀`,
`D = (K_d + K_D)/ω₀` (`Params.swing_iff` at each instant). -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem modulated_iff (Ks Pm δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ) :
    (∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = Pm t - elecPower p Ks δ δ' t) ↔
      ∀ t, p.M * δ'' t + p.D * δ' t + Ks t * δ t = Pm t :=
  forall_congr' fun t => (frozen p Ks t).swing_iff (δ t) (δ' t) (δ'' t) (Pm t)

/-! ## The period energy balance in the report's variables -/

/-- The electrical energy over a period: `∫₀ᴸ ΔP_e Δω = ∫₀ᴸ ΔP_m Δω − K_D ∫₀ᴸ Δω²` for an
`L`-periodic solution with `L`-periodic `C¹` synchronizing coefficient. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem electrical_energy (hω₀ : p.ω₀ ≠ 0) {L : ℝ}
    {Ks Ks' Pm δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hKs : ∀ t, HasDerivAt Ks (Ks' t) t) (hKs' : Continuous Ks')
    (hPm : Continuous Pm) (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t) (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = Pm t - elecPower p Ks δ δ' t)
    (hδL : Periodic δ L) (hKsL : Periodic Ks L) :
    ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, elecPower p Ks δ δ' t * speedDev p δ' t =
      (∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, Pm t * speedDev p δ' t) -
        p.KD * ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, speedDev p δ' t ^ 2 := by
  have heq' := (modulated_iff Ks Pm δ δ' δ'').mp heq
  have hδc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ t).continuousAt
  have hδ'c := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ' t).continuousAt
  have hKsc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hKs t).continuousAt
  have hbal := ParametricResonance.EnergyBalance.energy_balance hδ hδ' hKs hKs' hPm heq' hδL hKsL
  have hsp := ParametricResonance.EnergyBalance.integral_stiffness_power hδ hδ'c hKs hKs' hδL hKsL
  have e1 : ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, elecPower p Ks δ δ' t * speedDev p δ' t =
      p.ω₀⁻¹ * (∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, Ks t * δ t * δ' t) +
        p.Kd / p.ω₀ ^ 2 * ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, δ' t ^ 2 := by
    rw [← intervalIntegral.integral_const_mul, ← intervalIntegral.integral_const_mul,
      ← intervalIntegral.integral_add ((by fun_prop : Continuous _).intervalIntegrable _ _)
        ((by fun_prop : Continuous _).intervalIntegrable _ _)]
    congr 1; funext t
    simp only [elecPower, speedDev, frozen, Params.Pe]
    field_simp
  have e2 : ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, Pm t * speedDev p δ' t =
      p.ω₀⁻¹ * ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, Pm t * δ' t := by
    rw [← intervalIntegral.integral_const_mul]
    congr 1; funext t
    simp only [speedDev]
    field_simp
  have e3 : ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, speedDev p δ' t ^ 2 =
      (p.ω₀ ^ 2)⁻¹ * ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, δ' t ^ 2 := by
    rw [← intervalIntegral.integral_const_mul]
    congr 1; funext t
    simp only [speedDev]
    field_simp
  rw [e1, e2, e3, hsp]
  have hD : p.D = (p.Kd + p.KD) / p.ω₀ := rfl
  rw [hD] at hbal
  field_simp
  field_simp at hbal
  linear_combination hbal

/-- A free oscillation (`ΔP_m = 0`) with `K_D = 0` has zero electrical energy over a period,
`∫₀ᴸ ΔP_e Δω = 0`, whether `K_s` is constant (natural) or periodically varying (parametric). -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem free_electrical_energy (hω₀ : p.ω₀ ≠ 0) (hKD : p.KD = 0)
    {L : ℝ} {Ks Ks' δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hKs : ∀ t, HasDerivAt Ks (Ks' t) t)
    (hKs' : Continuous Ks') (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t)
    (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = 0 - elecPower p Ks δ δ' t)
    (hδL : Periodic δ L) (hKsL : Periodic Ks L) :
    ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, elecPower p Ks δ δ' t * speedDev p δ' t = 0 := by
  rw [electrical_energy (Pm := fun _ => 0) hω₀ hKs hKs' continuous_const hδ hδ' heq hδL hKsL,
    hKD]
  simp

/-- Natural mechanism: with constant `K_s` and `ΔP_m = 0`, every nonconstant periodic solution of
(3-8)–(3-9) has zero damping ratio `ξ = 0` (any waveform). -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem natural_dampingRatio_eq_zero (hp : p.Pos) {T : ℝ}
    {δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t) (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = 0 - p.Pe (δ t) (δ' t / p.ω₀))
    (hT : 0 < T) (hδT : Periodic δ T) (hnc : ∃ t, δ t ≠ δ 0) : p.dampingRatio = 0 := by
  have heq' : ∀ t, p.M * δ'' t + p.D * δ' t + p.Ks * δ t = 0 := fun t =>
    (p.swing_iff (δ t) (δ' t) (δ'' t) 0).mp (heq t)
  have hD := ParametricResonance.EnergyBalance.natural_damping_eq_zero hδ hδ' heq' hT hδT hnc
  have hsum : p.Kd + p.KD = 0 := by
    have : (p.Kd + p.KD) / p.ω₀ = 0 := hD
    rcases div_eq_zero_iff.mp this with h | h
    · exact h
    · exact absurd h hp.ω₀.ne'
  rw [Params.dampingRatio_eq hp, hsum, zero_div]

/-- Parametric mechanism in the report's variables (`ΔP_m = 0`): the damping power balances the
pump power of the synchronizing coefficient, `(K_d + K_D) ∫₀ᴸ Δω² = (1/(2ω₀)) ∫₀ᴸ K̇_s Δδ²`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem parametric_power_balance (hω₀ : p.ω₀ ≠ 0) {L : ℝ}
    {Ks Ks' δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hKs : ∀ t, HasDerivAt Ks (Ks' t) t) (hKs' : Continuous Ks')
    (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t) (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = 0 - elecPower p Ks δ δ' t)
    (hδL : Periodic δ L) (hKsL : Periodic Ks L) :
    (p.Kd + p.KD) * ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, speedDev p δ' t ^ 2 =
      (∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, Ks' t * δ t ^ 2) / (2 * p.ω₀) := by
  have heq' := (modulated_iff Ks (fun _ => 0) δ δ' δ'').mp heq
  have h := ParametricResonance.EnergyBalance.parametric_balance hδ hδ' hKs hKs' heq' hδL hKsL
  have e3 : ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, speedDev p δ' t ^ 2 =
      (p.ω₀ ^ 2)⁻¹ * ∫ t in (0 : ℝ)..L, δ' t ^ 2 := by
    rw [← intervalIntegral.integral_const_mul]
    congr 1; funext t
    simp only [speedDev]
    field_simp
  have hD : p.D = (p.Kd + p.KD) / p.ω₀ := rfl
  rw [e3]
  rw [hD] at h
  field_simp
  field_simp at h
  linear_combination -h

/-! ## The forced response for comparison -/

/-- Forced sinusoidal steady state with constant `K_s` (phasors of `OscillationPhasor`): the mean
mechanical power input balances the damping power, `Re(F W̄) = (K_d + K_D) |W|²`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem forced_power_phasor (hω₀ : p.ω₀ ≠ 0) (Ω : ℝ) (Dδ : ℂ) :
    (p.mechPhasor Ω Dδ * conj (p.freqPhasor Ω Dδ)).re =
      (p.Kd + p.KD) * ‖p.freqPhasor Ω Dδ‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [Complex.sq_norm]
  simp only [Params.mechPhasor, Params.freqPhasor, Params.M, Params.D, Complex.mul_re,
    Complex.mul_im, Complex.add_re, Complex.add_im, Complex.ofReal_re, Complex.ofReal_im,
    Complex.I_re, Complex.I_im, Complex.conj_re, Complex.conj_im, Complex.normSq_apply, map_mul]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- Forced sinusoidal steady state with constant `K_s`: the angle amplitude is linear in the
mechanical power amplitude, `|D| = |F| / |K_s − MΩ² + jΩD|`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem forced_amplitude {Ω : ℝ} {Dδ : ℂ}
    (hc : ((p.Ks - p.M * Ω ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) + ((Ω * p.D : ℝ) : ℂ) * I ≠ 0) :
    ‖Dδ‖ = ‖p.mechPhasor Ω Dδ‖ / ‖((p.Ks - p.M * Ω ^ 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) + ((Ω * p.D : ℝ) : ℂ) * I‖ := by
  rw [Params.mechPhasor, norm_mul, mul_div_cancel_left₀ _ (norm_ne_zero_iff.mpr hc)]

/-! ## The phase-angle method on a parametric oscillation -/

/-- Over the period `L` the in-phase products of the harmonics of `ΔP_e` and `Δω` sum to zero for
every free oscillation with `K_D = 0`: `Σ_k Re(P_k W̄_k) = 0`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem inPhase_hasSum_zero (hω₀ : p.ω₀ ≠ 0) (hKD : p.KD = 0)
    {L : ℝ} (hL : 0 < L) {Ks Ks' δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hKs : ∀ t, HasDerivAt Ks (Ks' t) t)
    (hKs' : Continuous Ks') (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t)
    (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = 0 - elecPower p Ks δ δ' t)
    (hδL : Periodic δ L) (hKsL : Periodic Ks L) :
    HasSum (fun k => (coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') k *
      conj (coeff hL (speedDev p δ') k)).re) 0 := by
  have hδc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ t).continuousAt
  have hδ'c := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ' t).continuousAt
  have hKsc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hKs t).continuousAt
  have hP : Continuous (elecPower p Ks δ δ') := by
    show Continuous fun t => Ks t * δ t + p.Kd * (δ' t / p.ω₀); fun_prop
  have hW : Continuous (speedDev p δ') := by
    show Continuous fun t => δ' t / p.ω₀; fun_prop
  have h := ParametricResonance.Wirtinger.hasSum_re_coeff_mul_conj hL hP hW
  rwa [free_electrical_energy hω₀ hKD hKs hKs' hδ hδ' heq hδL hKsL, mul_zero] at h

/-- The phase-angle method on a sustained free oscillation with `K_D = 0` (natural or
parametric): the in-phase part `|P₁| |W₁| cos φ₁` of the fundamental (`φ₁` the angle by which
`P₁` lags `W₁`) is bounded by the mean and harmonic tail of `ΔP_e` and `Δω`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem parametric_inPhase_le (hω₀ : p.ω₀ ≠ 0) (hKD : p.KD = 0)
    {L : ℝ} (hL : 0 < L) {Ks Ks' δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hKs : ∀ t, HasDerivAt Ks (Ks' t) t)
    (hKs' : Continuous Ks') (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t)
    (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = 0 - elecPower p Ks δ δ' t)
    (hδL : Periodic δ L) (hKsL : Periodic Ks L) :
    |‖coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') 1‖ * ‖coeff hL (speedDev p δ') 1‖ *
        Real.cos (lagAngle (coeff hL (speedDev p δ') 1) (coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') 1))| ≤
      ‖coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') 0‖ * ‖coeff hL (speedDev p δ') 0‖ / 2 +
        ∑' n : ℕ, ‖coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') ((n : ℤ) + 2)‖ *
          ‖coeff hL (speedDev p δ') ((n : ℤ) + 2)‖ := by
  have hδc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ t).continuousAt
  have hδ'c := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ' t).continuousAt
  have hKsc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hKs t).continuousAt
  have hP : Continuous (elecPower p Ks δ δ') := by
    show Continuous fun t => Ks t * δ t + p.Kd * (δ' t / p.ω₀); fun_prop
  have hW : Continuous (speedDev p δ') := by
    show Continuous fun t => δ' t / p.ω₀; fun_prop
  have h := ParametricResonance.Wirtinger.abs_re_coeff_one_le hL hP hW
    (free_electrical_energy hω₀ hKD hKs hKs' hδ hδ' heq hδL hKsL)
  set P := coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') 1
  set W := coeff hL (speedDev p δ') 1
  have hc : ‖P‖ * ‖W‖ * Real.cos (lagAngle W P) = (P * conj W).re := by
    have := Complex.norm_mul_cos_arg (W * conj P)
    rw [norm_mul, Complex.norm_conj] at this
    rw [lagAngle, mul_comm ‖P‖, this, ← Complex.conj_re, map_mul, Complex.conj_conj, mul_comm]
  rw [hc]
  exact h

/-- A half-frequency oscillation (`δ` and `K_s`, `δ(t + T) = −δ(t)`, `K_s(t + T) = K_s(t)`): over
`L = 2T` the means of `ΔP_e` and `Δω` vanish and the in-phase part of the fundamental is bounded by
the harmonic tail alone, `|P₁| |W₁| |cos φ₁| ≤ Σ_{k ≥ 2} |P_k| |W_k|`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem halfFrequency_inPhase_le (hω₀ : p.ω₀ ≠ 0) (hKD : p.KD = 0)
    {T : ℝ} (hL : 0 < 2 * T) {Ks Ks' δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hKs : ∀ t, HasDerivAt Ks (Ks' t) t)
    (hKs' : Continuous Ks') (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t)
    (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t = 0 - elecPower p Ks δ δ' t)
    (hanti : Antiperiodic δ T) (hKsT : Periodic Ks T) :
    |‖coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') 1‖ * ‖coeff hL (speedDev p δ') 1‖ *
        Real.cos (lagAngle (coeff hL (speedDev p δ') 1) (coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') 1))| ≤
      ∑' n : ℕ, ‖coeff hL (elecPower p Ks δ δ') ((n : ℤ) + 2)‖ *
          ‖coeff hL (speedDev p δ') ((n : ℤ) + 2)‖ := by
  have hδc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ t).continuousAt
  have hδ'c := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hδ' t).continuousAt
  have hKsc := continuous_iff_continuousAt.2 fun t => (hKs t).continuousAt
  have hW : Continuous (speedDev p δ') := by
    show Continuous fun t => δ' t / p.ω₀; fun_prop
  have hδL := hanti.periodic_two_mul
  have hKsL : Periodic Ks (2 * T) := by rw [two_mul]; exact hKsT.add_period hKsT
  have hanti' := ParametricResonance.Wirtinger.antiperiodic_of_hasDerivAt hδ hanti
  have hW0 : coeff hL (speedDev p δ') 0 = 0 := by
    rw [coeff_eq_integral]
    simp only [kernelExp, Int.cast_zero, mul_zero, zero_div, neg_zero, zero_mul,
      Complex.exp_zero, one_mul]
    rw [intervalIntegral.integral_ofReal,
      ParametricResonance.Wirtinger.integral_antiperiodic_eq_zero hW
        (fun t => by simp only [speedDev, hanti' t, neg_div]),
      Complex.ofReal_zero, mul_zero]
  have h := parametric_inPhase_le hω₀ hKD hL hKs hKs' hδ hδ' heq hδL hKsL
  rwa [hW0, norm_zero, mul_zero, zero_div, zero_add] at h

/-! ## The necessary modulation depth -/

/-- The undamped natural frequency `ω_n = √(ω₀ K_s / (2H))` of (3-10). -/
def natFreq (p : Params) : ℝ := Real.sqrt (p.ω₀ * p.Ks / (2 * p.H))

/-- `ξ / ω_n = D / (2 K_s)` with `D = (K_d + K_D)/ω₀`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem dampingRatio_div_natFreq (hp : p.Pos) :
    p.dampingRatio / natFreq p = p.D / (2 * p.Ks) := by
  have hH := hp.H
  have hω := hp.ω₀
  have hK := hp.Ks
  have h1 : Real.sqrt (2 * p.H * p.ω₀ * p.Ks) * Real.sqrt (p.ω₀ * p.Ks / (2 * p.H)) =
      p.ω₀ * p.Ks := by
    rw [← Real.sqrt_mul (by positivity),
      show 2 * p.H * p.ω₀ * p.Ks * (p.ω₀ * p.Ks / (2 * p.H)) = (p.ω₀ * p.Ks) ^ 2 by
        field_simp, Real.sqrt_sq (by positivity)]
  have h2 : 0 < Real.sqrt (p.ω₀ * p.Ks / (2 * p.H)) := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr (by positivity)
  have h3 : 0 < Real.sqrt (2 * p.H * p.ω₀ * p.Ks) := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr (by positivity)
  rw [Params.dampingRatio_eq hp, natFreq, Params.D, div_div, mul_assoc, h1]
  field_simp

/-- The necessary modulation depth of a sustained half-frequency oscillation: under
`K_s(t) = K_s (1 + ε cos Ωt)` and `ΔP_m = 0`, a nonzero `(2π/Ω)`-antiperiodic solution of
(3-8)–(3-9) (an oscillation at `Ω/2`) needs `|ε| ≥ ξ Ω / ω_n`, for every depth. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem halfFrequency_depth_ge (hp : p.Pos) {ε Ω : ℝ} (hΩ : 0 < Ω)
    {δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t) (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t =
      0 - elecPower p (fun s => p.Ks * (1 + ε * Real.cos (Ω * s))) δ δ' t)
    (hanti : Antiperiodic δ (2 * Real.pi / Ω)) (hne : ∃ t, δ t ≠ 0) :
    p.dampingRatio * Ω / natFreq p ≤ |ε| := by
  have heq' := (modulated_iff _ (fun _ => 0) δ δ' δ'').mp heq
  have h := ParametricResonance.Wirtinger.pump_amplitude_cos (m := p.M) hΩ hp.Ks hδ hδ' heq'
    hanti hne
  rw [mul_div_right_comm, dampingRatio_div_natFreq hp, div_mul_eq_mul_div]
  exact h

/-- At the 2:1 resonance `Ω = 2ω_n` the necessary depth is `|ε| ≥ 2ξ`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem halfFrequency_depth_ge_two (hp : p.Pos) {ε : ℝ}
    {δ δ' δ'' : ℝ → ℝ} (hδ : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ (δ' t) t) (hδ' : ∀ t, HasDerivAt δ' (δ'' t) t)
    (heq : ∀ t, 2 * p.H / p.ω₀ * δ'' t + p.KD / p.ω₀ * δ' t =
      0 - elecPower p (fun s => p.Ks * (1 + ε * Real.cos (2 * natFreq p * s))) δ δ' t)
    (hanti : Antiperiodic δ (2 * Real.pi / (2 * natFreq p))) (hne : ∃ t, δ t ≠ 0) :
    2 * p.dampingRatio ≤ |ε| := by
  have hH := hp.H
  have hω := hp.ω₀
  have hK := hp.Ks
  have hn : 0 < natFreq p := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr (by positivity)
  have h := halfFrequency_depth_ge hp (by positivity) hδ hδ' heq hanti hne
  rwa [mul_div_assoc, mul_div_cancel_right₀ _ hn.ne', mul_comm] at h

/-! ## The first-order boundary from the 2:1 averaging theorems -/

section FirstOrder

open powerlib.ParametricResonance.BlockAveraging (physJ physLeft physRight modX expS)

/-- The first-order family at `ε` (pump frequency `2ν₀`): the report's parameters with inertia
`H`, frequency `ω₀`, `K_D = 0`, damping torque coefficient `K_d = 4εHν₀ξ̂` and mean synchronizing
coefficient `K_s = (2H/ω₀) ν₀² (1 − 2εd̂)`. -/
def famParams (H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε : ℝ) : Params :=
  ⟨H, ω₀, 0, 2 * H / ω₀ * ν₀ ^ 2 * (1 - 2 * ε * dh), 4 * ε * H * ν₀ * ξh⟩

/-- The family's synchronizing coefficient `K_s(t) = (2H/ω₀) ν₀² (1 − 2εd̂ + εη̂ cos 2ν₀t)`. -/
def famKs (H ω₀ ν₀ dh ηh ε t : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  2 * H / ω₀ * ν₀ ^ 2 * (1 - 2 * ε * dh + ε * ηh * Real.cos (2 * ν₀ * t))

/-- The critical state matrix `A₀c = !![0, 1; −ν₀², 0]` (natural frequency at half the pump
frequency, no damping). -/
def critMatrix (ν₀ : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ := !![0, 1; -ν₀ ^ 2, 0]

/-- The first-order change `A₀' = !![0, 0; 2ν₀²d̂, −2ν₀ξ̂]` (detuning and damping). -/
def shiftMatrix (ν₀ ξh dh : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ :=
  !![0, 0; 2 * ν₀ ^ 2 * dh, -(2 * ν₀ * ξh)]

/-- The modulation `A₁ = !![0, 0; −ν₀²η̂, 0]`, `Re{A₁ e^{j2ν₀t}} = A₁ cos 2ν₀t`. -/
def pumpMatrix (ν₀ ηh : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ :=
  !![0, 0; -((ν₀ ^ 2 * ηh : ℝ) : ℂ), 0]

/-- Real modal coordinates of `A₀c`: `x = P y`, `P = diag(1, −ν₀)` (no stable remainder). -/
def modalP (ν₀ : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 0) ℝ := Matrix.fromCols !![1, 0; 0, -ν₀] 0

/-- `Q = P⁻¹ = diag(1, −1/ν₀)`. -/
def modalQ (ν₀ : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin 2 ⊕ Fin 0) (Fin 2) ℝ := Matrix.fromRows !![1, 0; 0, -ν₀⁻¹] 0

variable {H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ηh : ℝ}

/-- The family's state matrix of (3-10) is `A₀c + ε (A₀' + Re{A₁ e^{j2ν₀t}})`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem fam_stateMatrix (hH : H ≠ 0) (hω₀ : ω₀ ≠ 0) (ε t : ℝ) :
    (frozen (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε) (famKs H ω₀ ν₀ dh ηh ε) t).stateMatrix =
      physJ (critMatrix ν₀) (shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh) (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh) (2 * ν₀) ε t := by
  rw [Params.stateMatrix_eq]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
    simp [physJ, modX, critMatrix, shiftMatrix, pumpMatrix, frozen, famParams, famKs, Params.M,
      Params.D, -Complex.ofReal_mul, -Complex.ofReal_pow] <;>
    field_simp <;> ring

@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] private theorem modalP_mul_modalQ (hν : ν₀ ≠ 0) :
    modalP ν₀ * modalQ ν₀ = 1 := by
  rw [modalP, modalQ, Matrix.fromCols_mul_fromRows, Matrix.zero_mul, add_zero]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two, hν]

@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] private theorem modalQ_mul_modalP (hν : ν₀ ≠ 0) :
    modalQ ν₀ * modalP ν₀ = 1 := by
  ext (i | i) (j | j)
  · fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
      simp [modalP, modalQ, Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two, hν]
  · exact j.elim0
  · exact i.elim0
  · exact i.elim0

@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] private theorem modalQ_crit_modalP (hν : ν₀ ≠ 0) :
    modalQ ν₀ * critMatrix ν₀ * modalP ν₀ =
      fromBlocks (ParametricResonance.TwoToOne.base 0 (2 * ν₀ / 2)) 0 0 0 := by
  ext (i | i) (j | j)
  · fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
      simp [modalP, modalQ, critMatrix, ParametricResonance.TwoToOne.base, Matrix.mul_apply,
        Fin.sum_univ_two]
    field_simp
  · exact j.elim0
  · exact i.elim0
  · exact i.elim0

@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] private theorem physLeft_modalQ :
    physLeft (modalQ ν₀) = ![1 / 2, -(I / 2) * (ν₀⁻¹ : ℝ)] := by
  funext j
  fin_cases j <;>
    simp [physLeft, modalQ, Matrix.vecMul, dotProduct, Fintype.sum_sum_type,
      ParametricResonance.TwoToOne.left]

@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] private theorem physRight_modalP :
    physRight (modalP ν₀) = ![1, (ν₀ : ℂ) * I] := by
  funext j
  fin_cases j <;>
    simp [physRight, modalP, Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Fintype.sum_sum_type,
      ParametricResonance.TwoToOne.right]

/-- The first-order eigenvalue shift in the modal coordinates of `A₀c`:
`λ₁ = u A₀' r = −ν₀ξ̂ − jν₀d̂` (damping rate `εν₀ξ̂`, frequency shift `−εν₀d̂`). -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem shift_fam (hν : ν₀ ≠ 0) :
    physLeft (modalQ ν₀) ⬝ᵥ ((shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh).map (algebraMap ℝ ℂ) *ᵥ
        physRight (modalP ν₀)) = -((ν₀ * ξh : ℝ) : ℂ) - ((ν₀ * dh : ℝ) : ℂ) * I := by
  have hν' : (ν₀ : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hν
  rw [physLeft_modalQ, physRight_modalP]
  simp [shiftMatrix, Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]
  field_simp
  ring_nf
  rw [I_sq]
  ring

/-- The pump coefficient in the modal coordinates of `A₀c`: `g = u A₁ r̄ = jν₀η̂/2`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem pump_fam (hν : ν₀ ≠ 0) :
    physLeft (modalQ ν₀) ⬝ᵥ (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh *ᵥ star (physRight (modalP ν₀))) =
      ((ν₀ * ηh / 2 : ℝ) : ℂ) * I := by
  have hν' : (ν₀ : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hν
  rw [physLeft_modalQ, physRight_modalP]
  simp [pumpMatrix, Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]
  field_simp

@[tmio T, powerlib_foundation] private theorem spectralRadius_fin_zero
    (A : Matrix (Fin 0) (Fin 0) ℂ) : spectralRadius ℂ A < 1 := by
  rw [spectrum.SpectralRadius.of_subsingleton]
  exact zero_lt_one

/-- First-order boundary, stability: for `ξ̂ > 0` and `η̂² < 16(ξ̂² + d̂²)` every Floquet multiplier
of the family's swing model (state `(Δδ, Δδ̇)`, period `2π/(2ν₀)`) lies inside the unit circle for
all small `ε > 0` (`BlockAveraging.physical_stable`). -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem firstOrder_stable (hH : H ≠ 0) (hω₀ : ω₀ ≠ 0) (hν : 0 < ν₀)
    (hξ : 0 < ξh) (hg : ηh ^ 2 < 16 * (ξh ^ 2 + dh ^ 2)) :
    ∀ᶠ ε in 𝓝[>] (0 : ℝ), ∀ (μ : ℂ) (v : Fin 2 → ℂ), v ≠ 0 →
      (Periodic.monodromy
          (fun t => (frozen (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε) (famKs H ω₀ ν₀ dh ηh ε) t).stateMatrix)
          (2 * Real.pi / (2 * ν₀)) 0).map (algebraMap ℝ ℂ) *ᵥ v = μ • v → ‖μ‖ < 1 := by
  have hs : (physLeft (modalQ ν₀) ⬝ᵥ ((shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh).map (algebraMap ℝ ℂ) *ᵥ
      physRight (modalP ν₀))).re < 0 := by
    rw [shift_fam hν.ne']
    simp only [Complex.sub_re, Complex.neg_re, Complex.ofReal_re, Complex.mul_re,
      Complex.ofReal_im, Complex.I_re, Complex.I_im, mul_zero, mul_one, sub_zero]
    nlinarith
  have hg' : ‖physLeft (modalQ ν₀) ⬝ᵥ (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh *ᵥ star (physRight (modalP ν₀))) / 2‖ ^ 2 <
      ‖physLeft (modalQ ν₀) ⬝ᵥ ((shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh).map (algebraMap ℝ ℂ) *ᵥ
        physRight (modalP ν₀))‖ ^ 2 := by
    rw [shift_fam hν.ne', pump_fam hν.ne', Complex.sq_norm, Complex.sq_norm]
    simp [Complex.normSq_apply]
    nlinarith [sq_pos_of_pos hν]
  have h := ParametricResonance.BlockAveraging.physical_stable (by positivity : (0 : ℝ) < 2 * ν₀)
    (modalP_mul_modalQ hν.ne') (modalQ_mul_modalP hν.ne') 0 (modalQ_crit_modalP hν.ne')
    (shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh) (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh) hs hg' (spectralRadius_fin_zero _)
  filter_upwards [h] with ε hε
  rw [show (fun t => (frozen (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε) (famKs H ω₀ ν₀ dh ηh ε) t).stateMatrix) =
      physJ (critMatrix ν₀) (shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh) (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh) (2 * ν₀) ε from
    funext fun t => fam_stateMatrix hH hω₀ ε t]
  exact hε

/-- First-order boundary, parametric instability: for `16(ξ̂² + d̂²) < η̂²` the family's swing
model has a Floquet multiplier outside the unit circle for all small `ε > 0`
(`BlockAveraging.physical_unstable`). -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem firstOrder_unstable (hH : H ≠ 0) (hω₀ : ω₀ ≠ 0) (hν : 0 < ν₀)
    (hg : 16 * (ξh ^ 2 + dh ^ 2) < ηh ^ 2) :
    ∀ᶠ ε in 𝓝[>] (0 : ℝ), Periodic.FloquetUnstable
      (fun t => (frozen (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε) (famKs H ω₀ ν₀ dh ηh ε) t).stateMatrix)
      (2 * Real.pi / (2 * ν₀)) := by
  have hg' : ‖physLeft (modalQ ν₀) ⬝ᵥ ((shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh).map (algebraMap ℝ ℂ) *ᵥ
        physRight (modalP ν₀))‖ ^ 2 <
      ‖physLeft (modalQ ν₀) ⬝ᵥ (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh *ᵥ star (physRight (modalP ν₀))) / 2‖ ^ 2 := by
    rw [shift_fam hν.ne', pump_fam hν.ne', Complex.sq_norm, Complex.sq_norm]
    simp [Complex.normSq_apply]
    nlinarith [sq_pos_of_pos hν]
  have h := ParametricResonance.BlockAveraging.physical_unstable
    (by positivity : (0 : ℝ) < 2 * ν₀) (modalP_mul_modalQ hν.ne') (modalQ_mul_modalP hν.ne') 0
    (modalQ_crit_modalP hν.ne') (shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh) (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh) hg'
    (spectralRadius_fin_zero _)
  filter_upwards [h] with ε hε
  rw [show (fun t => (frozen (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε) (famKs H ω₀ ν₀ dh ηh ε) t).stateMatrix) =
      physJ (critMatrix ν₀) (shiftMatrix ν₀ ξh dh) (pumpMatrix ν₀ ηh) (2 * ν₀) ε from
    funext fun t => fam_stateMatrix hH hω₀ ε t]
  exact hε

/-- The family's damping ratio (3-11): `ξ = εξ̂ / √(1 − 2εd̂)`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem famParams_dampingRatio (hH : 0 < H) (hω₀ : 0 < ω₀)
    (hν : 0 < ν₀) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 2 * ε * dh < 1) :
    (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε).dampingRatio = ε * ξh / Real.sqrt (1 - 2 * ε * dh) := by
  have hpos : (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε).Pos :=
    ⟨hH, hω₀, by simp only [famParams]; have : 0 < 1 - 2 * ε * dh := by linarith
                 positivity⟩
  have h1 : 0 < 1 - 2 * ε * dh := by linarith
  rw [Params.dampingRatio_eq hpos]
  simp only [famParams]
  rw [show 2 * H * ω₀ * (2 * H / ω₀ * ν₀ ^ 2 * (1 - 2 * ε * dh)) =
      (2 * H * ν₀) ^ 2 * (1 - 2 * ε * dh) by field_simp,
    Real.sqrt_mul (by positivity), Real.sqrt_sq (by positivity)]
  have := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr h1
  field_simp
  ring

/-- The family's natural frequency: `ω_n = ν₀ √(1 − 2εd̂)`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem famParams_natFreq (hH : H ≠ 0) (hω₀ : ω₀ ≠ 0)
    (hν : 0 < ν₀) (ε : ℝ) :
    natFreq (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε) = ν₀ * Real.sqrt (1 - 2 * ε * dh) := by
  simp only [natFreq, famParams]
  rw [show ω₀ * (2 * H / ω₀ * ν₀ ^ 2 * (1 - 2 * ε * dh)) / (2 * H) =
      ν₀ ^ 2 * (1 - 2 * ε * dh) by field_simp,
    Real.sqrt_mul (sq_nonneg _), Real.sqrt_sq hν.le]

/-- The family's modulation in the report's relative form: `K_s(t) = K_s (1 + η cos 2ν₀t)` with
relative depth `η = εη̂ / (1 − 2εd̂)`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem famKs_eq (hω₀ : ω₀ ≠ 0) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 2 * ε * dh ≠ 1)
    (t : ℝ) :
    famKs H ω₀ ν₀ dh ηh ε t = (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε).Ks *
      (1 + ε * ηh / (1 - 2 * ε * dh) * Real.cos (2 * ν₀ * t)) := by
  have h1 : 1 - 2 * ε * dh ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.mpr (Ne.symm hε)
  simp only [famKs, famParams]
  field_simp

/-- The family's TR-110 quantities are of first order in `ε`: as `ε → 0⁺`, `ξ/ε → ξ̂`, the
relative depth `η = εη̂/(1 − 2εd̂)` satisfies `η/ε → η̂`, and the pump detuning `d` defined by
`2ν₀ = 2ω_n(1 + d)` satisfies `d/ε → d̂`. -/
@[tmio M, powerlib_domain] theorem fam_firstOrder (hH : 0 < H) (hω₀ : 0 < ω₀) (hν : 0 < ν₀) :
    Tendsto (fun ε => (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε).dampingRatio / ε) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 ξh) ∧
    Tendsto (fun ε => ε * ηh / (1 - 2 * ε * dh) / ε) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 ηh) ∧
    Tendsto (fun ε => (ν₀ / natFreq (famParams H ω₀ ν₀ ξh dh ε) - 1) / ε) (𝓝[>] 0)
      (𝓝 dh) := by
  have hsmall : ∀ᶠ ε in 𝓝[>] (0 : ℝ), 0 < ε ∧ 2 * ε * dh < 1 := by
    have h1 : ∀ᶠ ε in 𝓝 (0 : ℝ), 2 * ε * dh < 1 :=
      (continuous_const.mul continuous_id |>.mul continuous_const).continuousAt.eventually_lt
        continuousAt_const (by simp)
    filter_upwards [self_mem_nhdsWithin, nhdsWithin_le_nhds h1] with ε hε h
    exact ⟨hε, h⟩
  have hc : ContinuousAt (fun ε : ℝ => 1 - 2 * ε * dh) 0 := by fun_prop
  have hq : Tendsto (fun ε : ℝ => 1 - 2 * ε * dh) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 1) := by
    have := hc.tendsto.mono_left (nhdsWithin_le_nhds (s := Ioi 0))
    simpa using this
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hlim : Tendsto (fun ε : ℝ => ξh / Real.sqrt (1 - 2 * ε * dh)) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 ξh) := by
      have := (tendsto_const_nhds (x := ξh)).div (hq.sqrt) (by simp)
      rw [Real.sqrt_one, div_one] at this
      exact this
    refine hlim.congr' ?_
    filter_upwards [hsmall] with ε ⟨hε, h⟩
    rw [famParams_dampingRatio hH hω₀ hν h]
    field_simp
  · have hlim : Tendsto (fun ε : ℝ => ηh / (1 - 2 * ε * dh)) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 ηh) := by
      have := (tendsto_const_nhds (x := ηh)).div hq one_ne_zero
      rw [div_one] at this
      exact this
    refine hlim.congr' ?_
    filter_upwards [hsmall] with ε ⟨hε, h⟩
    field_simp
  · have hd0 : HasDerivAt (fun ε : ℝ => 1 - 2 * ε * dh) (-(2 * dh)) 0 := by
      have := ((hasDerivAt_id (0 : ℝ)).mul_const (2 * dh)).const_sub 1
      convert this using 1
      · funext ε; simp; ring
      · simp
    have hd1 := (hd0.sqrt (by simp)).inv (by simp)
    have hslope := hd1.tendsto_slope_zero_right
    simp only [zero_add, mul_zero, zero_mul, sub_zero, Real.sqrt_one, one_pow,
      smul_eq_mul] at hslope
    have hval : -(-(2 * dh) / (2 * 1)) / 1 = dh := by ring
    rw [hval] at hslope
    refine hslope.congr' ?_
    filter_upwards [hsmall] with ε ⟨hε, h⟩
    rw [famParams_natFreq hH.ne' hω₀.ne' hν ε]
    have hs : 0 < Real.sqrt (1 - 2 * ε * dh) := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr (by linarith)
    show ε⁻¹ * ((Real.sqrt (1 - 2 * ε * dh))⁻¹ - (Real.sqrt (1 - 2 * 0 * dh))⁻¹) = _
    rw [mul_zero, zero_mul, sub_zero, Real.sqrt_one, inv_one]
    field_simp

end FirstOrder

end powerlib.Synchronous.ParametricSwing
